---
import AroundScreen from "./AroundScreen.astro";
import SourceBadge from "./SourceBadge.astro";
import { sidebars } from "./data";

interface Props { home: string; world: string; }
const { home, world } = Astro.props;
---
<section class="world-lab-screen" id="submit">
        <header class="world-lab-screen-head"><div><p class="hara-v2-kicker">Screen 05 · Submit source</p><h2>Community discovery starts with reviewable rules.</h2></div><p>Register an RSS feed, Substack publication, X account, subreddit, Hacker News domain, or GitHub repository, then preview what would match.</p></header>
        <div class="world-lab-canvas around-lab-canvas">
          <AroundScreen current="submit" mainId="around-submit-content" sidebarTitle="Source registration" sidebarGroups={sidebars.submit} sidebarNote="Submission proposes a source. Public ingestion begins only after adapter, ownership state, and match rule are visible." home={home} world={world}>
            <Fragment slot="actions"><a class="hara-v2-button" href="#radar">Cancel</a><a class="hara-v2-button">Save draft</a><a class="hara-v2-button" data-variant="primary" href="#source">Review source ↗</a></Fragment>
            <div class="around-heading"><div><p class="hara-v2-kicker">Step 01 of 04</p><h1>What should World watch?</h1><p>Start with the source itself. Matching and ownership remain separate.</p></div><span class="hara-v2-badge">Draft</span></div>
            <form class="around-panel around-form"><fieldset><legend>Source type</legend><div class="around-source-types"><label><input type="radio" name="type" checked /><SourceBadge source="substack" /><span>Publication feed</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="type" /><SourceBadge source="x" /><span>Account or list</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="type" /><SourceBadge source="reddit" /><span>Subreddit or search</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="type" /><SourceBadge source="github" /><span>Repository activity</span></label></div></fieldset><label><span>Publication or feed URL</span><div class="around-inline-field"><input value="https://systems-small.example/feed" /><button class="hara-v2-button">Inspect</button></div><small>Prototype only: no network request is made.</small></label><div class="around-form-grid"><label><span>Display name</span><input value="Systems in the Small" /></label><label><span>Submitted by</span><input value="@chris · GitHub verified" disabled /></label></div><label><span>Reason for inclusion</span><textarea>Technical essays about language runtimes, schemas, and durable work, with direct links to Hara repositories.</textarea></label><fieldset><legend>Initial match rule</legend><div class="around-rule"><span>Include when</span><select><option>an exact Hara entity appears</option></select><span>and</span><select><option>confidence is at least 0.82</option></select></div></fieldset></form>
            <section class="around-panel around-match-preview"><header class="around-section-head"><div><p class="hara-v2-kicker">Recent-entry preview</p><h2>Three matches, one rejection.</h2></div><button>Adjust rule</button></header><div><article data-match="true"><span>✓</span><p><b>Programming languages as inspectable worlds</b><small>Exact hara-lang.org link · 1.00</small></p></article><article data-match="true"><span>✓</span><p><b>The smallest useful durable-work interface</b><small>Known work.* namespace · 0.91</small></p></article><article data-match="true"><span>✓</span><p><b>Revision fences in browser runtimes</b><small>hara-wasm-core · 1.00</small></p></article><article><span>—</span><p><b>Notes on workflow tools</b><small>No Hara entity · 0.12</small></p></article></div></section>
            <Fragment slot="aside">
              <section class="hara-v2-panel"><header class="hara-v2-panel-header"><h2>Adapter status</h2></header><div class="hara-v2-panel-body around-status"><div><SourceBadge source="substack" /><span>RSS ready</span></div><div><SourceBadge source="x" /><span>credentialed</span></div><div><SourceBadge source="reddit" /><span>gated review</span></div><div><SourceBadge source="hacker-news" /><span>public API</span></div></div></section>
              <section class="hara-v2-panel"><header class="hara-v2-panel-header"><h2>Ownership</h2></header><div class="hara-v2-panel-body around-stack"><p>A submitter recommends a source. An owner can later claim it through proof.</p><span class="hara-v2-badge">Community recommended</span></div></section>
              <section class="hara-v2-panel"><header class="hara-v2-panel-header"><h2>Before activation</h2></header><div class="hara-v2-panel-body around-checks"><span>✓ Public source</span><span>✓ Adapter visible</span><span>✓ Matches previewed</span><span>○ Review pending</span></div></section>
            </Fragment>
          </AroundScreen>
        </div>
        <div class="world-lab-notes"><article><b>Source before content</b><p>World records where discovery comes from.</p></article><article><b>Preview before activation</b><p>Over-broad rules become visible early.</p></article><article><b>Recommendation is not ownership</b><p>Claiming control remains separately verified.</p></article></div>
      </section>
